<title>USA: KVH wins $3.4 mln U.S. Army contract.</title>
<headline>KVH wins $3.4 mln U.S. Army contract.</headline>
<dateline>MIDDLETOWN, R.I. 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>KVH Industries Inc said Thursday it has won a $3.4 million contract to manufacture TACNAV digital navigation systems for the U.S. Army's Bradley Fighting Vehicle.</p>
<p>Delivery is scheduled in the fourth quarter of 1997. The current $3.4 million option exercise, said the company, builds upon its original $4.5 million contract awarded in June.</p>
<p>KVH makes and sells digital navigation systems and mobile satellite communications systems for use in commercial, military, and marine applications.</p>
</text>
